      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "For example, DbgTrace (\"responseText =\" lines in regression test 39 (IO::Network::Transfer)  - produce large strings, and these display as garbage.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Debugging deeper and doing more DbgTrace calls I ran into frequent crashes.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "I thought it was bugs with SmallStackBuffer, or some such. but now. Just this.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Not super critical - but since it can be such a time waster, mark as pretty importnat (not regression I dont believe). NOT clear if its the trace handling or the Format() string code (which would make it a litle more importnat).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "In that format code - when trying to repridcue - try making the buffer smalle r(instaead of 10K try 10 bytes and then do resize loop on vsprint()).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
